Z||000005||XDrewX||12-02-2001||01:03 AM||||Heres my story, <P>I used to skate ALOT about 20 years ago, <BR>(god I feel old). <BR>I was good, real good, then I got into BMX.<P>Well my son skates now.<BR>Man have the boards changed.<BR>When I skated, We only had one "kick tail". and our trucks were wide as were our wheels.<P>Over the summer, I was going out to check the mail. Our mail boxes are centrally located, so it is about 200 feet from my curb.<P>Well I grabbed my sons board and headed out to the street.<BR>I jumped on the board and took off to the mail boxes.  I kind of surprised myself how comfortable I was after all the years of not skating.<BR>Well, <BR>All my sons friends were hanging out in front of the house, and thought that It was cool as S*it, that I could ride,<P>Heres the good part:<P>I got cockey and did a couple spins, then Decided I was going to ollie up onto the curb.<BR>I got some speed...........Ollied.......<BR>and firmly planted the front truck into the curb.<P>I hit the ground hard on my shoulder, and my mail went flying.<P>No injury, just some hurt pride.<P>In all this rambling I guess the feel good thing was that I could still ride the board and do a few tricks after not skating for many years.<P>If you want to hear another funny story, ask Me about going snow boarding last year.<P>Peace, <P>Andrew <BR>||||reg||1
